    "created_at": "2016-02-24T22:50:32Z",
    "updated_at": "2016-02-24T22:50:54Z",
    "body": "I created a fiddle: https://jsfiddle.net/11anLvjq/1/ to see what is shipping.\n\nIn Chrome, the viewBox attribute of the svg ends up being used as an intrinsic size for the image. Kinda makes sense, but this paradigm ignores the \"s\" in \"svg\". Also, the edges of the drawing are too blurry, which suggests the image was resampled, meaning the intermediate rasterization was probably done at another resolution.\n\nIn Firefox, the call to createPattern throws a NS_ERROR_NOT_AVAILABLE\n\nIE chokes at image load time. Have not figured out why. Probably some incompatible markup detail in the SVG file.\n",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
