    "created_at": "2016-03-04T13:59:07Z",
    "updated_at": "2016-03-04T14:59:46Z",
    "body": "For consistency with how SVG images are sized in every other image context (backgrounds, border-image, markers, shapes, etc) using the default sizing algorithm is the reasonable choice, with the canvas scratch bitmap size as the default object size.\n\nThat said, for patterns, it gets a bit silly since the pattern size will be a contain constraint resolved against the canvas size (given an intrinsic aspect ratio) and thus rather big for actual tiling on said canvas. Not sure if this is a real problem.\n\nUsing the viewBox for intrinsic size is unprecedented (usually it just provides aspect ratio) in other contexts as far as I know, and just something Blink and WebKit happens to do lacking other options historically.\n",
    "author_association": "NONE",
    "pin": null,
